Compare the difference between a shortbread cookie and that of biscotti. Shortbread cookies seem to almost melt in your mouth, where as[ bisc]otti has a much lower butter content and are hard and crunchy. If a cookie[ recipe] calls for butter, I’d use the butter, especially in cookies where butter is the[ flavor] of the cookie. On the other hand cookies such as Molasses or gingerbread, I[ wouldn]’t[ hesitate] to use shortening. Do not use “reduced fat” or whipped butter products when you bake cookies, they can contain up to 58% water.
